================================================================================
                    PROXY & CHROME ENVIRONMENT CHEAT SHEET
================================================================================
Host Target: {TARGET_HOST}
Deployment Date: {DEPLOY_DATE}

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. CURRENT PROXY STATUS & EXIT IPS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
* Native Machine IP:     {NATIVE_IP}
* Active Proxy Exit IP:  {ACTIVE_PROXY_IP} (Country: {ACTIVE_COUNTRY})
* HTTP Proxy Port:       http://127.0.0.1:{HTTP_PORT}
* SOCKS5 Proxy Port:     socks5h://127.0.0.1:{SOCKS_PORT}

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2. TERMINAL ON-DEMAND PROXY COMMANDS (Copy & Paste)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
[ENABLE PROXY in Current Terminal]:
  export http_proxy=http://127.0.0.1:{HTTP_PORT}
  export https_proxy=http://127.0.0.1:{HTTP_PORT}
  export all_proxy=http://127.0.0.1:{HTTP_PORT}

[TEST CURRENT IP]:
  curl https://api.ipify.org
  # Expected output: {ACTIVE_PROXY_IP}

[DISABLE PROXY in Current Terminal]:
  unset http_proxy https_proxy all_proxy

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
3. ISOLATED CHROME INSTANCES
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
{CHROME_INSTANCES_LIST}

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
4. SERVICE MANAGEMENT COMMANDS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
* Check Status:  systemctl status {SERVICE_NAME}
* Restart Proxy: systemctl restart {SERVICE_NAME}
* Stop Proxy:    systemctl stop {SERVICE_NAME}
* View Logs:     journalctl -u {SERVICE_NAME} -n 30 --no-pager

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
5. ANTI-LEAK HARDENING VERIFICATION
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
* QUIC (UDP 443): Disabled via --disable-quic
* WebRTC IP Leak: Restricted via --force-webrtc-ip-handling-policy=disable_non_proxied_udp
* DNS Leak:       Resolved remotely via HTTP CONNECT / --disable-features=DnsOverHttps
* Root Sandbox:   Safely adapted with --no-sandbox and --disable-dev-shm-usage
================================================================================
